Score left blank. RUBRIC-GAP / format not verified. I can't score the format part from the Citation Sheet, so I can't give a total.

(1) Currency (date). BMTC-15 shows a 'BMTC at a glance' page dated 'As on 25 September, 2026' (FY 2026-27). It gives Schedules 6248, Vehicles 6921 (Including EV), Daily Service kms 12.39 lakh, Trips 61740, Everyday Traffic Revenue Rs 7.28 crore, GCC e-buses 1771, Depots 50, Bus stations 48, Staff 28382 and Bus Staff Ratio 4.54. The page footer says 'Last Updated: 30-09-2026'. BMTC-14 ('Perfomance Indicator') lists 'Performance Indicators from 2018-19 to 2025-26( Estimated)'. It has a PDF link for Physical performance and an entry for Financial Performance. On date alone, this looks like it meets the condition for the current or previous year. But the 2025-26 figures are estimates, not actuals. And the at-a-glance page gives operating statistics with no benchmarks or targets.

(2) Format. This decides the score and cannot be confirmed. Step 2 describes the 0.5 band as 'structured HTML table/dashboard with downloadable data'. The at-a-glance figures are HTML text with no download link that I could see. The saved text can't show whether they sit in an HTML table. The multi-year Performance Indicators PDF (linked on BMTC-14) is not in the Citation Sheet, so I can't tell whether it is a text or scanned PDF. Step 2 says the 0 band lists only scanned reports and images. If so, a text PDF or an HTML table without a download fits no band.

(3) I searched the Citation Sheet for a dashboard, CSV/XLS or open-data release, or an annual report. I found none from BMTC. BMTC-02 (RTC Act, 1950) only requires an annual report to the State Government. BMTC-28 lists line-checking reports (latest seen dated 2024). These are older than the current or previous FY.

A reviewer should:
- open the Physical and Financial Performance Indicators PDFs on BMTC-14 and check whether they are text or scanned, and which FY has actual figures;
- check whether BMTC-15 uses an HTML table and offers any download;
- confirm whether operating statistics count as 'performance information' and whether 'Estimated' figures count;
- capture dated screenshots.

The full Detailed Methodology text was not provided to me. Band descriptions come from Step 2's account of it.

I left the score blank. The Citation Sheet does not show a citizen-participation provision for BWSSB plans. It also does not cover every legal layer, so I cannot confirm that none exists. Not found is not the same as absent. I checked the Step 2 answer against the sources, and the sources support it.

What I read:
(1) BWSSB Act 1964 (BWSSB-02, PRS-republished text, as amended up to the 2010-2021 amending Acts). Section 15(2)(b)-(c) makes it the Board's duty to prepare and carry out water supply and sewerage schemes. Under the proviso, schemes estimated at more than Rs 1 crore need State Government approval. No provision requires publishing a draft scheme, inviting objections or suggestions, or holding a hearing. Section 14(1) says the State Government 'shall constitute' a Consultative Committee: Board members plus 3 to 9 persons appointed after consulting bodies representing the municipal corporation (the Act still names it the Bruhat Bangalore Mahanagara Palike), the Bangalore City Improvement Trust Board and 'consumers of water'. Under s.14(4)(i) its role is 'to advise the Board on major questions of policy and major schemes'. It is Government-appointed and advisory. It is not a process open to citizens.
(2) GBA Act 2024 (BWSSB-04, Act 36 of 2025, PRS text, GBA era). Public objections or suggestions appear in other places only:
- the gazette notification process for area changes (pp. 8-9);
- the heritage list (s.297(2));
- Ward Sabha inputs to the ULG's Annual Ward Development Plan (s.103(1)(c)).
None of these applies to BWSSB's water or sewerage plans. Under s.14(2)(c) the BMPC prepares a draft development plan, but the excerpt I could read does not show a public-objection step that covers BWSSB schemes.
(3) A sheet-wide search for 'public consultation draft plan objections suggestions citizens' found nothing BWSSB-specific.

Missing from the Citation Sheet, which is why affirmative absence for a 0 is not met:
- the Rules under BWSSB Act s.87 (s.14(4)(iv) lets Rules add matters for the Consultative Committee);
- BWSSB Regulations under s.88;
- the Karnataka Town and Country Planning Act 1961;
- any state water or sewerage policy requiring consultation;
- the full text of GBA Act s.14(2)(c).

If the scorer decides an appointed advisory committee with consumer-interest members counts as 'participation' for a partial band, the s.14 provision would be the evidence for it. That is a methodological call for the team. I could not check the band structure myself because the full Detailed Methodology text was not provided. The Act still names the BBMP and the City Improvement Trust Board, and no official source in the sheet shows successor bodies substituted for them. Flagged for the team.
